Z||000000||jlruiz67||08-26-2000||12:48 AM||||If you have done a engine conversion, could you share with us the cost (money) of the conversion? would you do it again? what would you do different? Recomendations would be appreciated. Thank you ||||reg||14
Z||000001||rprevo||08-26-2000||07:39 AM|||| <BR>I did mine for 4800 bucks and that included<BR>my paint and a ton of labor cause I made<BR>everything for the conversion. <BR>  If you would like to<BR>here about them Ask and I'll tell you.<BR>It's alot of typeing. <P> Ray<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||terryk||08-26-2000||11:30 AM||||I've done a couple and my rule of thumb is $1000 over the cost of the engine just for parts and fabricate. Time is 100 hours of labor. <P>You can see where the cost will be $5000-6000 over the cost of the engine.<P>IMHO<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||ourufo||08-26-2000||12:56 PM||||I dont rember how much it cost me after buing Archie's basic kit. count on extra for the donuts and coffie for the guys at the parts store.You'll be going there often.<P>------------------<BR>OURUFOV8||||reg||6
Z||000004||ThatRickGuy||08-27-2000||02:12 PM||||~$1700 (including tax) for a beef up and rebuild of the 2.8(3.1). The best thing about it, No Extra Parts!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> true, you can get a crate 3.4 for ~$1700, but it'll take a bunch more to actually get it in.||||reg||1
Z||000005||jlruiz67||08-27-2000||04:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ThatRickGuy:<BR><B>~$1700 (including tax) for a beef up and rebuild of the 2.8(3.1). The best thing about it, No Extra Parts!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> true, you can get a crate 3.4 for ~$1700, but it'll take a bunch more to actually get it in.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>What do you mean by a bunch more to acrually get it in? It was my impression that the only thing that had to be done was to relocate the starter. In my book that's not a bunch. Could you elaborate? Thanks<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000006||ThatRickGuy||08-28-2000||07:40 AM||||Well, with a pre '88 automatic, you'll also need a new fly wheel, the starter relocated, and part of the block ground off to fit the auto tranny. Unless you have the proper tools and a good hand, you'll have to get that stuff done for ya, which I would guess would be atleast around $200. Plus, puting the 3.4 crate in a mid engine vehicle voids the warrenty. so, yeah it's not all "that much" but, for a warrenty on a dayly driver, the 3.1 conversion just makes scense. Sorry if my post sounded negative or anything, it's been a very strange weekend.||||reg||1
